  "summary": "Telegram-controlled remote shell and host exfiltration in infogram-bot",
  "details": "infogram-bot registers Telegram message handlers that forward received message text into subprocess.check_output(cmd, shell=True, cwd=cwd, timeout=120) on the installer's host, giving any authorized Telegram user ID full arbitrary command execution on the machine running the bot. Additional handlers (dumpall/takeall) build `tar -czf... -C {target}.` archives of arbitrary paths (default `/`) and upload them via Telegram reply_document; a `getall` handler archives the current working directory; `.printenv` joins and returns all `os.environ` entries; `.grep` scans environment variables and the filesystem for operator-supplied patterns. The Telegram bot API endpoint is the command-and-control and exfiltration channel, and the bot process on the installer's host is the persistent access point.",
